# ONNX Runtime reduced operator build configuration
#
# Only the operators used by the target model(s) are kept in the build, which
# drastically reduces libonnxruntime.so size.
#
# IMPORTANT: the model(s) must run with graph optimization DISABLED at runtime
# (e.g. ORT_DISABLE_ALL). The reduced-op build whitelists kernels per domain;
# with graph optimization enabled, fusions would introduce ops (Gemm,
# FusedMatMul, ...) that are not listed here, and the session would fail with
# ORT_NOT_IMPLEMENTED.
#
# If the model changes, regenerate this list by inspecting the model:
#   python -c "import onnx; m=onnx.load('model.onnx'); print(sorted({n.op_type for n in m.graph.node}))"
#
# Format: <domain>;<opset>;<op1,op2,...>
ai.onnx;17;Add,ArgMax,Cast,Concat,Constant,Conv,Expand,Gather,GRU,MatMul,MaxPool,Mul,Relu,Reshape,Shape,Softmax,Tanh,Transpose,Unsqueeze
